  "body": "**Blocked by:** none\n\n## Context\nReview of pull request #418 found that `close()` in `backend/packages/realtime-client/src/syncClient.ts` (currently around lines 238-244) clears the reconnect timer and calls `socket.close()`, but never resets `reconnectAttempt` to `0`. Only `ws.onopen` resets it. If a caller calls `close()` and a later reconnect path reads `reconnectAttempt` before the next successful `onopen`, the stale attempt count from the previous connection's backoff is used.\n\n## Task\n- In `close()` in `backend/packages/realtime-client/src/syncClient.ts`, reset `reconnectAttempt` to `0` alongside clearing the reconnect timer and calling `socket.close()`.\n\n## Touches\n- backend/packages/realtime-client/src/syncClient.ts (the `close()` method only)\n- backend/packages/realtime-client/src/__tests__/syncClient.unit.test.ts (one new test case for the reset)\n\n## Scope\n### In scope\n- Resetting `reconnectAttempt` inside `close()`.\n\n### Out of scope\n- Any other reset or backoff logic in `syncClient.ts`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- After calling `close()`, `reconnectAttempt` is `0`, verified directly or through its effect on the next reconnect delay.\n\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=418 key=fb04caddb1 -->\n",
